@title Cross references fade only where they overlap, and come back on selection (1366x768)
@area Schematic
@sizes 1366x768
# -K1's table is held by hand on a wire; -K2's table is free. Shift+X once: "fade on overlap" fades only -K1's table, -K2's stays clear. Selecting -K1 brings its table back. The status bar chip names the mode.
open qa/fixtures/references-overlap.kopercad
wait 30
shot full
key shift+x
wait 20
shot fade-on-overlap
click 389 222
wait 30
shot crossed-table-selected-is-clear
key escape
wait 10
key shift+x
wait 20
shot all-faded
check_layout
